Thanks Ash for checking the samples shared and providing the Mule-side confirmation.

From the BICoE perspective, our understanding is:
1. Cross-day duplicates: For the sample reviewed, Mule confirmed that the message was sent towards Event Hub, but due to the timeout the expected success/deletion status was not captured on the Mule side. As a result, the message remained in the Blob/replay path and was replayed later. On the BICoE side, this can create a cross-day duplicate which may fall outside the current deduplication window and propagate into downstream Gold / DIM Audit Rate Permission data. This scenario therefore needs to be considered as part of the duplicate-handling solution.
2. Residual orphan records: For the orphan samples reviewed, Mule confirmed that the available Blob data had already been replayed and that there were no additional follow-up messages present in Blob for those Quote IDs. From the BICoE side, this indicates that the remaining orphan cases are not caused by the current Blob replay mechanism. The daily orphan count has reduced significantly, which is positive, but the remaining occurrences now need a separate end-to-end investigation to understand where the missing messages are being lost before they reach Blob/replay.
